# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft
Feature: Container Booking Limit

  Scenario Outline: A container can have only one active booking
    Given a gate slot tomorrow at <time> with room for 2 trucks
    And I am a driver
    When I book that slot for a valid container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "the booking is confirmed with a reference"

    Examples:
      | time        | container |
      | 10:00       | A123456   |

    Scenario Outline: Booking another slot for an already booked container is refused
    Given a gate slot tomorrow at <time> with room for 2 trucks
    And I am a driver
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "the booking is confirmed with a reference"
    And another driver books a different slot for the same container
    Then their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

    Examples:
      | time        | container |
      | 10:00       | A123456   |

    Scenario Outline: Booking an already booked container after cancellation
    Given a gate slot tomorrow at <time> with room for 2 trucks
    And I am a driver
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "the booking is confirmed with a reference"
    And another driver looks up my booking
    Then they are told it does not exist
    And I cancel my booking
    Then my booking is "CANCELLED"
    And I am a driver
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "the booking is confirmed with a reference"

    Examples:
      | time        | container |
      | 10:00       | A123456   |
